==Bulgarian==
{{wikipedia|lang=bg}}

===Etymology===
Akin to {{cog|cu|Дꙋнавъ}}, {{m|cu|Дѹнавъ}}, from {{inh|bg|sla-pro|*Dunavь}}, from {{der|bg|got|*𐌳𐍉𐌽𐌰𐍅𐌹}}, from {{der|bg|gem-pro|*Dōnawjaz}}, from {{der|bg|cel-pro|*Dānowyos}} (whence also {{m|la|Danubius}}), an extended form of the river-name {{m|cel-pro|*Dānu}}, from {{der|bg|ine-pro|*déh₂nu||river goddess}}, akin to {{m|ine-pro|*dʰenh₂-||to set in motion; to flow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{bg-IPA|Ду́нав}}

===Proper noun===
{{bg-proper noun|Ду́нав|m}}

# {{place|bg|t1=Danube|the second-longest <<river>> in <<cont/Europe>>, flowing through 10 countries: <<c/Germany,Austria,Slovakia,Hungary,Croatia,Serbia,Bulgaria,Romania,Moldova,Ukraine>>}}

====Inflection====
{{bg-ndecl|Ду́нав<(v)/n:sg/def:+>}}

